@startuml
title Kernel microstep automaton and macrostep boundaries
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Draining the token queue" as Drain #E9F5EA {
  state "Enter phase\n(enter_node: join acceptance,\ninstantiation, suspension, effects)" as Enter #DCEEFF
  state "Route phase\n(route_token: trigger filter,\nguards, selection, fan-out)" as Route #DCEEFF
  [*] --> Enter : pop token (FIFO)
  Enter --> Route : pass-through, join merge,\nor observation applied
  Route --> Enter : transition selected\n(child tokens enqueued)
}

state "KernelOutcome::Effects\n(pending activity or lifecycle effects)" as Effects #FFF0D9
state "KernelOutcome::Guards\n(Rholang guard needs on-chain observation)" as Guards #FFF0D9
state "KernelOutcome::Suspended\n(waits pending; ledger publishes due_at)" as SuspendedOut #FFE0C8
state "KernelOutcome::Cancelled" as CancelledOut #E7DCF5
state "KernelOutcome::Completed\n(sequence-ordered output value)" as CompletedOut #D9EFDF

Drain --> Effects : queue drained,\npending effects exist
Drain --> Guards : Route token blocked on an\nunobserved guard (requeued at FRONT)
Drain --> SuspendedOut : queue drained, no effects\nor guards, waits pending
Drain --> CancelledOut : queue drained,\ncancellation in progress
Drain --> CompletedOut : queue drained,\nnothing pending
Effects --> Drain : signed activity observation applied
Guards --> Drain : guard observation applied
SuspendedOut --> Drain : authenticated command applied\n(claim, apply, advance)

note right of Drain #EAF7EE
One pop is one microstep; a macrostep is the maximal
run of microsteps ending in a KernelOutcome, bounded
defensively by <latex>10^{6}</latex> steps. Outcome precedence:
Effects, then Guards, then a hard error if the queue is
blocked, then Suspended, Cancelled, Completed.
end note
note bottom of Guards #FFF3C9
External stimuli are admitted only between macrosteps.
There is no internal event queue: dispositions are
consumed by the producing token's own routing, never
broadcast. Every macrostep boundary is a durable
checkpoint opportunity.
end note
@enduml
